{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b8e2a4b0-1a2b-4c3d-9e5f-url-shortener-01",
    "name": "URL Shortener - Enterprise (Greenfield & Brownfield)",
    "description": "Reviewer-facing Postman collection for the url-shortener take-home exercise. Two independent flows:\n\n- **Greenfield**: exercises V2 directly as if it were the only system that ever existed (no V1 framing) - the shape of the API surface a true greenfield build would present.\n- **Brownfield**: exercises V1 first as the pre-existing baseline, then represents a 'V2 cutover' commit and shows how the Gateway's routing behaves for a brand-new V2 code before and after it has been read directly against V2 - reproducing the documented cache-as-index defect live (see 'Known defect' in infra/k8s/README.md).\n\nRun '0. Auth' once first to obtain a token; every other request reuses it via the {{accessToken}} collection variable. Import the companion environment file (url-shortener-enterprise.postman_environment.json) and select it before running - it covers both Option A (docker-compose + mvn spring-boot:run) and Option B (k3d) since both expose the same localhost ports (see README.md \"For reviewers: setup and verification\").",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Auth",
      "description": "Obtains a Keycloak access token for the 'urlshortener' realm using the Resource Owner Password Credentials grant, and stores it as a collection variable ({{accessToken}}) so every V2 request below can reuse it. Run this request first.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get access token (Resource Owner Password grant)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/urlshortener/protocol/openid-connect/token",
              "host": [
                "{{keycloakUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "realms",
                "urlshortener",
                "protocol",
                "openid-connect",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "grant_type",
                  "value": "password"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_id",
                  "value": "{{clientId}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "client_secret",
                  "value": "{{clientSecret}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{keycloakUsername}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{keycloakPassword}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Uses the 'urlshortener-client' confidential client against the realm imported at cluster/stack startup (infra/k8s/13-keycloak.yaml or the docker-compose Keycloak service). Set keycloakUsername/keycloakPassword in the environment to a real user of that realm before running."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Token endpoint returns 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response contains an access_token', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (body.access_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.access_token);",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "// Decode the JWT payload (no signature check - this is a reviewer",
                  "// convenience, not a security check) to surface the issuer being",
                  "// used, which matters for the Keycloak KC_HOSTNAME fix documented",
                  "// in infra/k8s/README.md and ARCHITECTURE.md.",
                  "if (body.access_token) {",
                  "    const payloadB64 = body.access_token.split('.')[1];",
                  "    const decoded = JSON.parse(atob(payloadB64.replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')));",
                  "    console.log('Token issuer (iss):', decoded.iss);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Greenfield - V2 as the primary system",
      "description": "Exercises V2 directly, treating it as the only system in existence - no V1 fallback framing, matching this project's own stance that V1 is a didactic 'legacy' simulation and a real greenfield build would only ever have V2. Covers create/redirect, custom alias, duplicate alias (409), reserved slug (400), invalid input (400), expiration (410), device-classified redirect rules, and the async bulk submit+poll flow. Run '0. Auth' first.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create short link (V2)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{v2Url}}/api/v2/urls",
              "host": [
                "{{v2Url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v2",
                "urls"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"longUrl\": \"https://www.anthropic.com/claude-code\",\n  \"expiresAt\": null\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Baseline V2 create, exercised as if V2 were the only system (no V1 fallback framing)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Create returns 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Response has a shortCode', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('shortCode');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "if (body.shortCode) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('gfShortCode', body.shortCode);",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Redirect via V2 directly (302)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{v2Url}}/{{gfShortCode}}",
              "host": [
                "{{v2Url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "{{gfShortCode}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "V2's redirect endpoint is public (no token) and returns 302 FOUND with a Location header."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Redirect returns 302', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(302);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Location header points at the original longUrl', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.eql('https://www.anthropic.com/claude-code');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "protocolProfileBehavior": {
            "followRedirects": false
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Redirect via Gateway (routes to V2)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/{{gfShortCode}}",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "{{gfShortCode}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Soft assertion: accepts 302 or 404. A fresh V2 code can 404 here until read once directly against V2, because the Gateway currently uses ShortLinkCache (a TTL'd read-through cache) as if it were a durable ownership index. See the 'Known defect' section in infra/k8s/README.md."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Gateway resolves the V2 code', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([302, 404]);",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 302) {",
                  "    pm.test('Location header matches the original longUrl', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.eql('https://www.anthropic.com/claude-code');",
                  "    });",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.warn('Gateway returned 404 for a fresh V2 code - this is the ",
                  "documented cache-as-index defect (see README.md \"Known defect\"). Run ",
                  "\"Redirect via V2 directly\" above first to warm the cache, then retry.');",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "protocolProfileBehavior": {
            "followRedirects": false
          }
        },
